From: Arvind Yadav <arvind.yadav.cs@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/xe/vm: Read bo resource under reservation in snapshot capture

xe_vm_snapshot_capture() dereferences bo->ttm.resource without holding the
bo reservation. This is both a NULL dereference and a use-after-free.

xe_ttm_bo_purge() purges with an empty ttm_placement, so ttm_bo_validate()
takes the ttm_bo_pipeline_gutting() path, which frees the resource via
ttm_resource_free() and leaves bo->ttm.resource NULL. The purged bo stays
mapped in the VM by design: xe_vm_populate_validate() skips re-populating
it and xelp_pte_encode_bo() maps it to scratch with XE_PTE_NULL. The VMA is
never removed, so the devcoredump walk still reaches it.

An already purged bo therefore oopses deterministically on the switch, and
a bo purged concurrently with the walk is a use-after-free even if the
pointer tested non-NULL first. Userspace only needs madvise(DONTNEED) on a
mapped bo followed by a hang, so an unprivileged process can use this for a
denial of service.

Read the resource under dma_resv_trylock() instead. A blocking
dma_resv_lock() is not an option here for two independent reasons: the
capture runs inside the dma_fence_begin_signalling() section opened by
devcoredump_snapshot(), and vm->snap_mutex, already held here, is itself
taken under the bo reservation on the gpuva insert/remove paths, so
blocking would invert that order.

When the trylock fails the memory region is left unknown. That costs only
a printed annotation, since uapi_mem_region is consumed solely by
xe_vm_snapshot_print(), which already special-cases -1. The data itself is
still captured by the delayed phase, where ttm_bo_access() revalidates
bo->resource under the reservation and returns -ENODATA if it is gone.

A bo found purged under the lock records -ENODATA immediately, which
matches the existing fallback branch and avoids a pointless kvmalloc of
the VMA length in xe_vm_snapshot_capture_delayed(). Both consumers already
handle an error pointer.

Note this also changes the reported region for a mem_type outside the
switch, such as XE_PL_STOLEN, from 0 to unknown. Previously such a bo was
silently reported as system memory because uapi_mem_region was left at its
kvzalloc() value.

Signed-off-by: Arvind Yadav <arvind.yadav.cs@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c
index 9e0176861c..5bcc760afd 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c
@@ -4526,17 +4526,43 @@ struct xe_vm_snapshot *xe_vm_snapshot_capture(struct xe_vm *vm)
 			snap->snap[i].cpu_caching = bo->cpu_caching;
 			snap->snap[i].bo = xe_bo_get(bo);
 			snap->snap[i].bo_ofs = xe_vma_bo_offset(vma);
-			switch (bo->ttm.resource->mem_type) {
-			case XE_PL_SYSTEM:
-			case XE_PL_TT:
-				snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 0;
-				break;
-			case XE_PL_VRAM0:
-				snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 1;
-				break;
-			case XE_PL_VRAM1:
-				snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 2;
-				break;
+			snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = -1;
+
+			/*
+			 * bo->ttm.resource is only stable under the bo
+			 * reservation, which xe_ttm_bo_purge() holds while
+			 * freeing it. Only a trylock is permitted here: this
+			 * runs inside a dma-fence signalling critical section,
+			 * and vm->snap_mutex is itself taken under the
+			 * reservation on the gpuva insert/remove paths.
+			 *
+			 * If the lock is unavailable the memory region stays
+			 * unknown, which costs only a printed annotation. The
+			 * data is captured later by xe_bo_read(), and
+			 * ttm_bo_access() revalidates the resource under the
+			 * reservation.
+			 */
+			if (dma_resv_trylock(bo->ttm.base.resv)) {
+				struct ttm_resource *res = bo->ttm.resource;
+
+				if (!res) {
+					/* Purged bo, nothing left to capture. */
+					snap->snap[i].data = ERR_PTR(-ENODATA);
+				} else {
+					switch (res->mem_type) {
+					case XE_PL_SYSTEM:
+					case XE_PL_TT:
+						snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 0;
+						break;
+					case XE_PL_VRAM0:
+						snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 1;
+						break;
+					case XE_PL_VRAM1:
+						snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 2;
+						break;
+					}
+				}
+				dma_resv_unlock(bo->ttm.base.resv);
 			}
 		} else if (xe_vma_is_userptr(vma)) {
 			struct mm_struct *mm =
